                                    }
                                ]
                            }
                        ]
                    },
                    {
                        "translation_id": "5617e61f-a478-4b48-96c1-5aa052fb7cd1",
                        "source_entry_id": "ef30683f-38af-345e-8f80-938d33ade2d4",
                        "target_lang_word": "seriously",
                        "target_lang_code": "en",
                        "target_sense_ids": [],
                        "cross_references": [
                            {
                                "target_word": "seriously",
                                "target_lang_code": "en",
                                "target_senses": [
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "deae5271-cb9a-30bd-beb9-a77903a51279",
                                        "entry_id": "9da9ac80-5e43-3f79-9b7f-7c43e9dea7c8",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "In a serious or literal manner."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "57392417-fc4f-42b9-b74d-651df7b4548c",
                                                "sense_id": "deae5271-cb9a-30bd-beb9-a77903a51279",
                                                "text": "He was hoping that we would take him seriously."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "1afed226-52ca-464b-a398-207d2ed59f33",
                                                "sense_id": "deae5271-cb9a-30bd-beb9-a77903a51279",
                                                "text": "Jimmy jokingly called Bob a doofus. Bob took the insult seriously."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "1c457da0-e05a-46ce-a71f-a5088e8e7603",
                                                "sense_id": "deae5271-cb9a-30bd-beb9-a77903a51279",
                                                "text": "“I’ll qualify the statement, then,” she answered, with a laugh. “We have known each other for two ages—hers and mine. But seriously we are as dear to each other as sisters, and now that I am going to lose her I am almost heartbroken.”"
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "34c956c3-5d8e-4465-8296-05892b09634c",
                                                "sense_id": "deae5271-cb9a-30bd-beb9-a77903a51279",
                                                "text": "Masters and Johnson wanted their work to be taken seriously, and wanted to stay a step ahead of the morality police, so they tended to write in almost comically dense medicalese."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "2385b71f-eefe-45b7-8e12-d5e7789b0f85",
                                                "sense_id": "deae5271-cb9a-30bd-beb9-a77903a51279",
                                                "text": "Jeremy, meanwhile, was the fun-lover, like me, who didn't always take it too seriously."
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    },
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "cfc7795f-2ac5-3971-8615-1eec4f26aa43",
                                        "entry_id": "9da9ac80-5e43-3f79-9b7f-7c43e9dea7c8",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "Gravely; deeply; very much."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "af27169b-3e5f-4ce9-937b-ac31ed10aa7e",
                                                "sense_id": "cfc7795f-2ac5-3971-8615-1eec4f26aa43",
                                                "text": "That was a seriously unpleasant thing to say."
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    },
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "eb1a2961-8e78-32b5-bb7d-24f545967377",
                                        "entry_id": "9da9ac80-5e43-3f79-9b7f-7c43e9dea7c8",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "Used to attempt to introduce a serious point in a less serious conversation."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "685ba981-657c-48fc-9d8d-cd233a162b9b",
                                                "sense_id": "eb1a2961-8e78-32b5-bb7d-24f545967377",
                                                "text": "Now, seriously, why did you forget to feed the cat today?"
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    },
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "7d3ef40f-a21c-33b1-b0f3-f111ae9f9124",
                                        "entry_id": "9da9ac80-5e43-3f79-9b7f-7c43e9dea7c8",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "Used to call back to a previous point, in disbelief or for emphasis."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "375f3e47-2794-44e7-a0aa-5e110d1631bc",
                                                "sense_id": "7d3ef40f-a21c-33b1-b0f3-f111ae9f9124",
                                                "text": "You baked ten (10) cakes. Seriously, why did you do that?"
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    },
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "cfc03800-9f78-3c7b-bc37-9bb323f820b5",
                                        "entry_id": "9da9ac80-5e43-3f79-9b7f-7c43e9dea7c8",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "In an extreme or major way; majorly."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [
                                            "informal"
                                        ],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "1a7953eb-d255-40b7-a3a6-017e0acfc8e3",
                                                "sense_id": "cfc03800-9f78-3c7b-bc37-9bb323f820b5",
                                                "text": "Unless you're seriously strapped (armed), you're about to be not okay too."
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    }
                                ]
                            }
                        ]
                    },
                    {
                        "translation_id": "95a8a822-9b08-41fc-b20c-ae1d8b100800",
                        "source_entry_id": "ef30683f-38af-345e-8f80-938d33ade2d4",
                        "target_lang_word": "soberly",
                        "target_lang_code": "en",
                        "target_sense_ids": [],
                        "cross_references": [
                            {
                                "target_word": "soberly",
                                "target_lang_code": "en",
                                "target_senses": [
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "6782ef86-d623-3ba5-ba02-d2aeb36c676d",
                                        "entry_id": "c556fbb5-8000-3ffc-adcc-5cd3eb78a648",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "In a sober manner; temperately; coolly; calmly; gravely; seriously."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "739d8a01-4f75-42a7-a2e2-afe15a3cf2f1",
                                                "sense_id": "6782ef86-d623-3ba5-ba02-d2aeb36c676d",
                                                "text": "Amongst this number of cordials and alteratives I do not find a more present remedy than a cup of wine or strong drink, if it be soberly and opportunely used."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "5633b79f-7765-4297-a45b-c1bbc5771442",
                                                "sense_id": "6782ef86-d623-3ba5-ba02-d2aeb36c676d",
                                                "text": "They gathered soberly in the farthest recess of the ward and gossiped about him in malicious, offended undertones, rebelling against his presence as a ghastly imposition and resenting him malevolently for the nauseating truth of which he was bright reminder."
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    }
                                ]
                            }
                        ]
                    },
                    {
                        "translation_id": "8c4d8339-3a45-4bf2-94ca-2e26724e3044",
                        "source_entry_id": "ef30683f-38af-345e-8f80-938d33ade2d4",
                        "target_lang_word": "solemnly",
                        "target_lang_code": "en",
                        "target_sense_ids": [],
                        "cross_references": [
                            {
                                "target_word": "solemnly",
                                "target_lang_code": "en",
                                "target_senses": [
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "c29bc2ae-12d9-3b48-b111-242cdd606167",
                                        "entry_id": "3488770f-c680-315c-9b89-57e4abcf4288",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "In a solemn manner."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "c8e71bb8-1911-4b18-a567-f01f7fabd78c",
                                                "sense_id": "c29bc2ae-12d9-3b48-b111-242cdd606167",
                                                "text": "And yet, though the happiness may be unenduring, what heart, though seared by time and worldly care, can fail to sympathise with those emotions of early life? In after years there are none such. They are the high noon of earthly joy. After them, life goes on decayingly and solemnly to its shadowy sunset."
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    }
                                ]
                            }
                        ]
                    },
